module chemiluminescenceDetection

manifest ParamagneticParticles
manifest TSH_Standard
manifest HRP_AntiTSH_Conjugate
manifest WashBuffer
manifest ParticleDiluent
manifest H2O2_StablePeroxide
manifest LuminolEnhancer

// ============================================================
// Automated Digital Microfluidic Platform for Magnetic-Particle-
// Based Immunoassays with Optimization by Design of Experiments
// Choi, Ng, Fobel, Chang-Yen, Yarnell, Pearson, Oleksak,
// Fischer, Luoma, Robinson, Audet, Wheeler
// Anal. Chem. 2013, 85, 9638-9646
// DOI: 10.1021/ac401847x
//
// ASSAY TARGET: Thyroid-Stimulating Hormone (TSH)
//   Clinically relevant range: 0 - 4 uIU/mL
//   LOD (optimized): 0.15 uIU/mL (screens for hyperthyroidism)
//
// PLATFORM DESCRIPTION:
//   Automated DMF platform (benchtop, ~18x23x30 cm enclosure)
//   featuring:
//     (a) 90 Pogo pin interface (15 inputs/sq in) for droplet
//         control via Microdrop + Arduino-based HV switching
//         (100-120 V_rms, 10 kHz sine wave AC).
//     (b) Integrated motorized Hamamatsu H10682-110 PMT
//         (5V DC, motor-driven engage/disengage, shutter).
//     (c) "Magnetic lens" assembly: neodymium bar (3 in x 1/2 in
//         x 1/4 in, mu_r=1.05, Br=1.32 T) flanked by two AISI
//         1080 steel machined armatures. Motor-driven vertical
//         engage (~150 um gap, ~600 uN vertical force) supports
//         up to 8 simultaneous parallel magnetic separations.
//
// DMF DEVICE:
//   Bottom plate: 80 actuation electrodes (2.2x2.2 mm each),
//   8 reagent reservoirs (16.4x6.7 mm), 4 waste reservoirs.
//   Interdigitated borders (140 um peak-to-peak sinusoids),
//   interelectrode gaps 30-80 um.
//   Unit droplet volume: ~800 nL.
//   Reservoir droplet volume: ~3.5 uL.
//
// OPTIMIZED PROTOCOL PARAMETERS (from 3^3 full factorial DOE):
//   Sample volume:          5 unit droplets (4 uL after merging)
//   Sample incubation time: 3 min
//   TSH standard conc:      0, 0.4, 4 uIU/mL
//   Conjugate mixing:       2 min
//   Wash cycles (step 1):   4x in wash buffer
//   Substrate mixing:       4 min
//   PMT integration:        10 s (stable signal window)
//
// REAGENT PREPARATION (off-chip, prior to loading):
//   - TSH standards (Abbott Labs) + Pluronic L64 0.05% v/v
//   - Particle working solution: ~3.0e8 particles/mL in
//     DMF-compatible particle diluent (pH 10: Tris base 6.1 g/L,
//     NaCl 5.8 g/L, BSA 1% w/v, thimerosal 0.05% w/v,
//     Pluronic L64 0.05% v/v)
//   - HRP-conjugated anti-TSH (Abcam, 2 ug/mL) in conjugate
//     diluent (DMF-compatible)
//   - SuperSignal ELISA Femto substrate (Thermo Fischer):
//     H2O2 stable peroxide + luminol-enhancer, each supplemented
//     with Pluronic L64 0.025% v/v
//   - DMF-compatible wash buffer
//
// MEASUREMENT NOTE:
//   A single stationary PMT services droplets sequentially.
//   To eliminate queue-wait signal decay (up to 45% signal
//   drop observed in pilot assays), wash buffer is removed
//   immediately after final wash, particles resuspended in
//   luminol-H2O2 substrate and mixed for 4 min to reach a
//   stable ~1-min measurement window before PMT engagement.
//
// DOE MODEL (eq 1, centered polynomial regression):
//   Factors: con (concentration), vol (sample volume),
//             inc (incubation time)
//   Response: Sqrt(SBR) [square-root of signal-to-background ratio]
//   Model fit: R^2=0.90, R^2_adj=0.88, RMSE=0.1597, p<0.0001
//   Key finding: longer incubation at high TSH REDUCES Sqrt(SBR);
//   optimum is 5 droplets x 3 min incubation.
//
// PERFORMANCE vs. PROTOTYPE (Ng et al., Anal. Chem. 2012):
//   CV:            6-10%    (was 9-21%)
//   LOD (abs):     0.6 nIU  (was 2.0 nIU,  3-fold improvement)
//   LOD (conc):    0.15 uIU/mL (was 0.83, 5-fold improvement)
//   Sample vol:    4.0 uL   (was 2.4 uL)
//   Incubation:    3 min    (was 6 min,  2-fold reduction)
//
// CFG STRUCTURE:
//   BB1  main              -- entry: reagent dispense, particle
//                             immobilization, sample incubation
//   BB2  washPass          -- washSignal > 0: particle pellets
//                             confirmed; proceed to conjugate step
//   BB3  washFail          -- washSignal <= 0: pellets lost; drain
//   BB4  washJoin          -- join: conjugate incubation begins
//   BB5  detectionPass     -- detectionSignal > 0: valid chemilum.
//                             signal; dispose substrate droplet
//   BB6  detectionFail     -- detectionSignal <= 0: no signal; drain
//   BB7  finalCleanup      -- terminal: dispose QC signals
// ============================================================

instructions:

// ============================================================
// BB1: main
// ============================================================

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 1: Dispense paramagnetic particle droplet from reservoir.
//   Working solution: ~3.0e8 particles/mL in DMF-compatible
//   particle diluent (pH 10). ~800 nL unit droplet.
//   Magnetic lens engages (motor, ~150 um gap) to pellet
//   particles on device surface; diluent droplet is moved away
//   (magnetic separation). Particle pellet remains immobilized.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

particleDrop    = dispense 1 units of ParamagneticParticles

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 2: Dispense 5 unit droplets of TSH standard.
//   Optimized DOE result: 5 pooled unit droplets (4 uL total)
//   yields highest Sqrt(SBR) at all tested concentrations.
//   TSH standards: 0, 0.4, or 4 uIU/mL (supplemented with
//   Pluronic L64 0.05% v/v for DMF compatibility).
//   Five droplets accumulated explicitly (BioScript compiler
//   requires scalar dispense + chained merge to accumulate
//   multi-unit volumes; multi-unit dispense does not produce
//   discrete indexed elements suitable for downstream ops).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

tsh1            = dispense 1 units of TSH_Standard
tsh2            = dispense 1 units of TSH_Standard
tsh3            = dispense 1 units of TSH_Standard
tsh4            = dispense 1 units of TSH_Standard
tsh5            = dispense 1 units of TSH_Standard

// Accumulate 5 unit droplets into a single pooled sample droplet.
tshPool_2       = mix tsh1 with tsh2 for 5s
tshPool_3       = mix tshPool_2 with tsh3 for 5s
tshPool_4       = mix tshPool_3 with tsh4 for 5s
tshSample       = mix tshPool_4 with tsh5 for 5s

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 3: Deliver pooled TSH sample to immobilized particles
//   and mix for 3 min (optimized incubation time from DOE).
//   Droplet shuttled in circular motion across 4+ electrodes
//   (continuous active mixing, 100-120 V_rms, 10 kHz) to
//   accelerate analyte binding to antibody-coated magnetic
//   particles. This replaces the 6 min incubation of the
//   prototype setup; rapid uniform mixing enables faster
//   binding kinetics.
//   DOE finding: con x inc interaction is negative at high TSH;
//   3 min at high vol outperforms 6-9 min at all concentrations.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

sampleIncubation = mix tshSample with particleDrop for 3m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 4: Wash particles 4 times in DMF-compatible wash buffer.
//   Magnetic lens engages to pellet particles; supernatant
//   droplet is moved to waste reservoir (magnetic separation).
//   Fresh wash buffer droplet moved over pellet; magnet
//   disengages; particles resuspend in wash buffer; repeat.
//   4 wash cycles remove unbound TSH and non-specific binders.
//   After wash 4, particles remain suspended in wash buffer
//   for conjugate delivery.
//
//   NOTE ON ABSTRACTION: Each wash cycle is modelled as a
//   sequential mix-with-wash-buffer operation. The magnetic
//   separation (pellet + supernatant removal) is a DMF-
//   specific hardware operation abstracted here as the mix
//   step completing and a new wash droplet being dispensed.
//   The magnetic lens facilitates up to 8 simultaneous
//   separations across the device.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Wash cycle 1
wash1a          = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash1b          = mix sampleIncubation with wash1a for 30s
washSup1        = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash1c          = mix wash1b with washSup1 for 10s
drain wash1c

// Wash cycle 2
wash2a          = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash2b          = mix wash1a with wash2a for 30s
washSup2        = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash2c          = mix wash2b with washSup2 for 10s
drain wash2c

// Wash cycle 3
wash3a          = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash3b          = mix wash2a with wash3a for 30s
washSup3        = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash3c          = mix wash3b with washSup3 for 10s
drain wash3c

// Wash cycle 4
wash4a          = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
wash4b          = mix wash3a with wash4a for 30s
washSup4        = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
particlesWashed = mix wash4b with washSup4 for 10s

// QC: confirm particle pellets are retained after wash series.
washSignal      = detect chemiluminescenceDetection on particlesWashed for 5s

// ============================================================
// BB2 / BB3: Wash / particle-retention QC gate
// Pass (BB2): washSignal > 0  -> particle pellets retained;
//             proceed to conjugate incubation.
// Fail (BB3): washSignal <= 0 -> pellets lost during wash;
//             drain and abort.
// Both branches converge at BB4 (washJoin).
// ============================================================

if (washSignal > 0) {
    dispose particlesWashed
} else {
    drain particlesWashed
}

// ============================================================
// BB4: washJoin
// Dispose wash QC signal. Control falls into conjugate
// incubation branch.
// ============================================================

dispose washSignal

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 5: Deliver HRP-conjugated anti-TSH detection antibody
//   and mix for 2 min.
//   Conjugate: HRP-conjugated mouse monoclonal anti-TSH
//   (Abcam, 2 ug/mL) in DMF-compatible conjugate diluent.
//   1 unit droplet (~800 nL) dispensed, moved over particle
//   pellet, and mixed for 2 min (active electrode mixing,
//   100-120 V_rms, 10 kHz). HRP-antibody binds to TSH
//   captured on the particle surface (sandwich formation).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

conjugateDrop   = dispense 1 units of HRP_AntiTSH_Conjugate
conjugateIncub  = mix wash4a with conjugateDrop for 2m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 6: Wash particles 4 times in DMF-compatible wash buffer
//   to remove unbound HRP-conjugate.
//   Paper specifies 5 washes in pilot protocol; optimized
//   protocol uses 4 washes (sufficient with improved mixing).
//   After the 4th wash, supernatant is removed IMMEDIATELY
//   (no queuing in wash buffer) to prevent signal decay.
//   Key optimization: eliminating the wash-buffer queue wait
//   that caused up to 45% signal drop in pilot assays.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// Wash cycle 1
cwash1a         = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
cwash1b         = mix conjugateIncub with cwash1a for 30s
cwashSup1       = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
cwash1c         = mix cwash1b with cwashSup1 for 10s
drain cwash1c

// Wash cycle 2
cwash2a         = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
cwash2b         = mix cwash1a with cwash2a for 30s
cwashSup2       = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
cwash2c         = mix cwash2b with cwashSup2 for 10s
drain cwash2c

// Wash cycle 3
cwash3a         = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
cwash3b         = mix cwash2a with cwash3a for 30s
cwashSup3       = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
cwash3c         = mix cwash3b with cwashSup3 for 10s
drain cwash3c

// Wash cycle 4 - FINAL: supernatant removed immediately.
cwash4a         = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
cwash4b         = mix cwash3a with cwash4a for 30s
cwashSup4       = dispense 1 units of WashBuffer
cwash4c         = mix cwash4b with cwashSup4 for 10s
drain cwash4c

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 7: Initiate chemiluminescent reaction immediately after
//   final wash (no delay).
//   (a) Resuspend particles in 1 unit (~800 nL) of H2O2
//       stable peroxide by disengaging magnetic lens and
//       moving H2O2 droplet over particle pellet.
//   (b) Merge and mix with 1 unit (~800 nL) of luminol-
//       enhancer solution for 4 min (optimized from pilot;
//       pilot used 40 s mix + 100 s incubation).
//       Active mixing drives HRP-catalysed luminol oxidation
//       and allows signal to reach a stable plateau.
//   Combined droplet: ~1600 nL pooled substrate.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

h2o2Drop        = dispense 1 units of H2O2_StablePeroxide
particlesInH2O2 = mix cwash4a with h2o2Drop for 10s

luminolDrop     = dispense 1 units of LuminolEnhancer
substratePool   = mix particlesInH2O2 with luminolDrop for 4m

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// STEP 8: PMT detection.
//   Motor lowers PMT to engaged position (shutter opens,
//   sensor positioned several hundred micrometers above
//   device surface). Chemiluminescent signal collected for
//   10 s within the stable measurement window (~1 min).
//   Signal proportional to HRP concentration (captured TSH).
//   Four replicates per concentration are averaged and fitted
//   to a linear calibration curve. LOD = mean(blank) + 3*SD(blank).
// ------------------------------------------------------------

detectionSignal = detect chemiluminescenceDetection on substratePool for 10s

// ============================================================
// BB5 / BB6: Detection QC gate
// Pass (BB5): detectionSignal > 0 -> valid chemiluminescent
//             signal above background; dispose substrate droplet.
// Fail (BB6): detectionSignal <= 0 -> no signal (reagent
//             failure or particle loss); drain.
// Both branches converge at BB7 (finalCleanup).
// ============================================================

if (detectionSignal > 0) {
    dispose substratePool
} else {
    drain substratePool
}

// ============================================================
// BB7: finalCleanup (terminal)
// Dispose PMT detection QC signal droplet.
// Experiment ends. PMT motor returns to disengaged position
// (shutter closes, ~5 cm above device surface).
// ============================================================

dispose detectionSignal

// [terminal -- no further instructions; exit node for CFG]
